    "title": "pandas.Index.get_indexer_for — pandas 2.3.3 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.get_indexer_for#\n\n- \n*final* Index.get_indexer_for(*target* )[source]#\n- Guaranteed return of an indexer even when non-unique. This dispatches to get_indexer or get_indexer_non_unique as appropriate. \n  - Returns:\n    - np.ndarray[np.intp]\n    - List of indices.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index([np.nan, 'var1', np.nan]) >>> idx.get_indexer_for([np.nan]) array([0, 2])",
